ios: login form (the keyboard opens by itself, 30 px field rows)

Logging in took a tap on New User or Existing User, then a tap on an 11 pt strip to bring up the keyboard:

- When the login form opens (the typing context goes from none to the username field), the keyboard is shown for the
  username at once (patch "keyboard-follows-input"'s sync). The native keyboard needs no user gesture. A connection
  that drops in game and logs in again shows the form's context too; that never raises the keyboard.
- The username and password fields take 30 px rows (upstream 15, about 11 pt on the phone): the username's grows
  upwards and the password's downwards, clear of the Login and Cancel buttons. The taps that select a field
  (titleScreenLoop) and the ones that raise the keyboard (insideLoginUser / insideLoginPass, now across the title box)
  use the same rows. Nothing is drawn differently.
- New User's hint says what the offline world needs: "New character: type any name. No password needed." (it said to
  choose a username and password; the host logs in with the name alone and fills a password in).

